1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,040
Offer reasons that are objective and data-based. They should support your suggestion or explain

2
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:12,200
your need. They help others understand why you think or feel as you do. They may persuade

3
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:16,960
others to your way of thinking or increase their willingness to meet your need. A common

4
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:22,680
error is to assume that the reasons that convince you must be equally convincing to others.

5
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:28,100
This isn't always the case. A reason can be absolutely true and supportive, yet not be

6
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:33,800
seen as important by someone else. In order to use reasoning more effectively, you'll

7
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:38,580
benefit from using the receptive behaviors to learn the other person's decision criteria

8
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:44,620
for a particular issue, or to understand what type of information he or she finds most persuasive.

9
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:49,620
Listen to the following examples. Then, come up with some reasons that support a suggestion

10
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:51,740
or need of your own.

11
00:00:51,740 --> 00:00:57,500
I have three reasons for suggesting this approach. First, it's recommended by the manufacturer.

12
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:04,019
Second, it's worked in the past. And third, we have two people who already know how to do it.

13
00:01:05,019 --> 00:01:10,140
Here's why I need the additional resources. The customer has asked us to move the project

14
00:01:10,140 --> 00:01:15,620
up by three months since we've agreed to provide educational benefits.

15
00:01:15,620 --> 00:01:19,620
It makes sense to put the Graduate School Catalog on our website.

